{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And his spirit was troubled.</b> Rashi explained: but regarding Nebuchadnezzar it is written ותתפעם רוחו, because there were two beatings — that he forgot the dream and the interpretation — whereas here he forgot only the interpretation. And even though it is written about Nebuchadnezzar חלום חלמתי ותפעם רוחי, there, that was after the magicians came before him, and there was only one beating there — for if the dream were known, the interpretation would be known to them, and therefore he forgot both the dream and the interpretation. And this one, who forgot only the interpretation — because Nebuchadnezzar's dream was for a long time, and had Daniel not told him the dream, he would not have believed him from the interpretation. But Pharaoh's dream was immediate, and he believed it. And the reason Nebuchadnezzar commanded to kill the magicians, as it is written ואמר להובדא לכל חכימי בבל — but Pharaoh did not say so — is because the magicians said to Nebuchadnezzar: How do you suppose we can tell you the dream? Are we prophets? As it is written מלתא די מלכא שאיל יקירא היא — meaning, it requires prophecy, as it is written ודבר ה׳ הי׳ יקר בימים ההם, ואחרן לא איתוהי קרי ביה ואהרן — meaning, Aaron is not here, the one who bears Urim and Thummim to reveal hidden things. Nebuchadnezzar said to them: You have reminded me of Urim and Thummim, and through the counsel of you priests who bear them, they have been lost from the world — by your lives, you shall be lost from the world. And therefore he commanded לאובדא יתהון."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {0 "The phrase ואחרן לא איתוהי קרי ביה ואהרן appears to be an Aramaic paraphrase of the biblical statement that the word of HaShem was rare in those days; the text is somewhat compressed and the syntax is difficult. The ending לאובדא יתהון is Aramaic for 'to destroy them.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:56.103127516Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}